On Mon, Mar 29, 2010 at 12:03 PM, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:

> Before you go further... your message gives the impression that it's common
> to see those things when it really is not at all.  I don't think I've ever
> seen these non-standard forms, but again, I'm still fairly new.


Except in examples, as in "It is permissable to place a "?" after the
question word as in {xu? do jimpe mi}, I've not once seen any character
other than the 26 letterals and 10 numerals used in written Lojban, i.e.:
abcdefgijklmnoprstuvxyz'.,1234567890


